research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-1843-          "fact": "L1",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-1844-          "source": "lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-1845-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-1846-          "quote": "Every Cauchy filter $\\mathcal F$ canonically determines a unique Cauchy filter $m(\\mathcal F)\\subseteq\\mathcal F$ that has no strictly coarser Cauchy filter. For every $x\\in X$, the principal filter $\\mathcal P_x:=\\{A\\subseteq X:x\\in A\\}$ is Cauchy and therefore has an associated minimal Cauchy filter $m(\\mathcal P_x)$.",
