research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4206-          "fact": "L2",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4207-          "source": "def-regular-and-t3-spaces",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4208-          "source_section": "Definition",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4209-          "quote": "**Regularity alone implies no other separation axiom.** It does not imply $T_0$,\n$T_1$ or Hausdorff ([[def-hausdorff-space]]): in the indiscrete topology on a set\n$X$ the only closed sets are $\\varnothing$ and $X$, so the only pair $(C, x)$ to\nbe separated has $C = \\varnothing$, and $U = X$, $V = \\varnothing$ separates it;\nyet no two distinct points are distinguished by any open set. Conversely $T_1$\ndoes not imply regularity. It is the *conjunction* $T_3$ that sits above\nHausdorff in the hierarchy, and the proof of that is three items below.",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4210-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4211-            "3.1"
