research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4215-          "fact": "L3",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json:4216:          "source": "lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4217-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4218-          "quote": "If $\\mathcal U$ is a uniformity on $X$, then its symmetric entourages form a filter base: for every $E\\in\\mathcal U$ there is a symmetric $D\\in\\mathcal U$ with $D\\subseteq E$. More generally, for every entourage $E$ and every integer $n\\ge 1$, there is a symmetric entourage $D$ whose $n$-fold composite satisfies $D^{\\circ n}\\subseteq E$.",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4219-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4220-            "1.1",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4221-            "2.1"
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4222-          ]
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4223-        },
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4224-        {
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4225-          "fact": "L3",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4226-          "source": "def-interior-closure-boundary-top",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4227-          "source_section": "Definition",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4228-          "quote": "- The **interior** of $A$ is\n  $\\operatorname{int}(A) := \\bigcup \\{\\, U \\in \\mathcal{T} : U \\subseteq A \\,\\}$.\n- The **closure** of $A$ is\n  $\\overline{A} := \\bigcap \\{\\, F \\subseteq X : F \\text{ closed and } A \\subseteq F \\,\\}$.\n- The **exterior** of $A$ is $\\operatorname{ext}(A) := \\operatorname{int}(X \\setminus A)$.\n- The **boundary** of $A$ is $\\partial A := \\overline{A} \\setminus \\operatorname{int}(A)$.\n- $x$ is a **limit point** (accumulation point) of $A$ if every neighbourhood $N$\n  of $x$ satisfies $N \\cap (A \\setminus \\{x\\}) \\ne \\varnothing$. The set of limit\n  points of $A$ is the **derived set** $A'$.\n- $x$ is an **isolated point of $A$** if $x \\in A$ and some neighbourhood $N$ of\n  $x$ satisfies $N \\cap A = \\{x\\}$.",
--
